id: pm-wa39rl
title: Completed-task transcripts accept terminal refusals and contradictory recovery metadata
description: "Greptile and CodeRabbit exact-head review on PR #1133 found that the public transcript parser can accept a task ending in refusal, successful steps can carry refusal-only metadata, and the retry-option fixture lacks its recovery_for edge. Enforce terminal-success topology and mutually exclusive refusal/recovery metadata in the SDK contract and replay corpus."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:contracts","area:sdk",recovery,review-feedback,testing
created_at: "2026-08-27T20:29:24.256Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-27T21:13:28.188Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#143da6b99c6d50ff73f411da"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Every completed task terminates in a non-refusal output; successful outputs reject refusal-only metadata; every corrected retry binds to the refusal it recovers; adversarial parser and replay regressions pass
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
expected_result: The public SDK transcript contract cannot represent an unsuccessfully terminated completed task or contradictory refusal metadata.
actual_result: The public transcript parser now rejects completed tasks whose terminal step is a refusal and rejects refusal-only metadata on successful steps; the canonical unknown-option retry is bound to refuse-option and replays through shell-free suggested_retry_args.
component: sdk-output-contracts
